# The input, fetched by `make` from github.com/arbace/slim-vim at the commit in
# upstream.sha.  Not tracked: this repository records WHICH slim-vim.c it was
# built from (upstream.sha, and its digest in slim.sha), as arbace/slim-vim
# records the upstream vim commit it was built from and not the tree.
slim-vim.c

# The products' binaries: the C product's, and the editor's, the core in Go.
slim-vim
whim-vim
/bin/

# The core half of whim-vim.c, cut at the first #include by `make editor.c`.
editor.c

# Boundaries an earlier pass left: a tar and a digest each.  Nothing produces
# them any more; `tools/st.sh build --to N` writes a tree when one is wanted.
.build/

# The recorded baselines every delta is measured against (`make whim-baselines`),
# which is the one produced thing worth keeping: nothing else can re-derive it.
.reference/

# The Go binary and the patched cc/v4 fork, content-keyed, plus what a sweep
# compiles: deleting it costs only the time to build again.
.cache/

# Every temporary goes here, not the shared /tmp: the Makefile exports
# TMPDIR to it, and worktrees go in .tmp/worktrees/.
.tmp/

# Editor swap files: vim names the first .swp and then walks backwards.
*.sw[a-p]

.claude/
